# Overview

This report documents the analysis pipeline that combines **two PCIC products** for the Vancouver / Pacific Northwest region:

1. **Gridded hydrologic model output** — multi-variable daily NetCDFs (BASEFLOW, RUNOFF, SWE, EVAP, SOIL_MOIST, plus glacier variables) at 1/16° resolution, 1945–2099.
2. **Station hydrologic model output** — daily streamflow time series at ~190 hydrometric gauges + dam sites in the Peace, Fraser, and Columbia basins, 1945–2099.

The two are joined to build a covariate-augmented annual block-maximum streamflow table suitable for **GEV (Generalised Extreme Value) modelling** of flood extremes.

> **Correction note.** An earlier version of this report described only the `BASEFLOW` workflow. The corrected version below reflects that the gridded dataset contains *multiple* variables and that the actual analysis uses both gridded covariates and station streamflow.

