# Output Products

| Stage | File | Contents |
|---|---|---|
| Station merge | `stream_coor_station_3_model.csv` | All stations × all dates × PNWNAmet + CanESM2 rcp45 + CanESM2 rcp85 + coords |
| Station split | `stream_coor_station_{hist,rcp45,rcp85}.csv` | Same, slimmed to one scenario each |
| Station blockmax | `sf_yearly_max_{hist,rcp45,rcp85}.csv` | Annual maximum daily streamflow per station |
| Gridded extract | `daily_bf_{hist,rcp45,rcp85}.tif` | Masked 5×5 neighbourhood baseflow grids (LZW-compressed) |
| Gridded summary | `avg_daily_bf_{hist,rcp45,rcp85}.parquet` | Per-station per-day **top-9 mean** representative baseflow |
| Final merge | `year_{hist,rcp45,rcp85}_sf_bf.csv` | GEV input: annual-max streamflow + same-day baseflow covariate |

> The same gridded pipeline can be re-run with a different `variable_name` (`runoff`, `swe`, `evap`, `soil_moist`, etc.) to add other covariates to the GEV table. Only the `variable_name` switch, the input NetCDF paths, and the output filenames need to change.

